dts: rk3576-armsom-sige5: describe the secure world

Adds the linaro,optee-tz firmware node the tee driver binds to, and
reservations covering the memory the secure world owns: upstream OP-TEE's
TZDRAM at 0x70000000, 32 MB, and its static shared memory at 0x72000000,
4 MB, from core/arch/arm/plat-rockchip/conf.mk.

Confirmed on hardware. Linux logs

  OF: reserved mem: ... nomap optee@70000000
  optee: revision 4.9, dynamic shared memory is enabled, initialized driver

giving /dev/tee0 and /dev/teepriv0. Before the firmware node existed,
/proc/device-tree/firmware held only scmi and the driver had nothing to bind
to.

All of it is inert in the default build, which ships no BL32: the SMC goes
unanswered so the driver never registers. Without the reservation Linux is
free to allocate over the secure world; it survived one boot here, which is
luck rather than a guarantee.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBGQqVfXFDyZYA6aV3X3Qq

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
@@ -1317,3 +1317,40 @@ rknpu_mmu: iommu@27702000 {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Secure world. Present only when the bootloader carries a BL32; a build
+ * without one leaves the SMC unanswered and the driver does not register,
+ * so these nodes are harmless either way.
+ *
+ * The reservations match the only secure world this system builds: upstream
+ * OP-TEE (USE_OPENSOURCE_TEE=1) at CFG_TZDRAM_START 0x70000000 with 32 MB and
+ * CFG_SHMEM_START 0x72000000 with 4 MB, from core/arch/arm/plat-rockchip/
+ * conf.mk. A bootloader carrying a secure world at some other address needs
+ * its own reservation to match.
+ */
+&{/} {
+	firmware {
+		optee {
+			compatible = "linaro,optee-tz";
+			method = "smc";
+		};
+	};
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/* TZDRAM, then the static shared memory */
+		optee@70000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x70000000 0x0 0x2000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		optee@72000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x72000000 0x0 0x400000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+};
